<Base title="Community Events" description="GEAR Moto Foundation's proposed rider community and fundraising events.">
<section class="inner-hero"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow">Community &amp; Connection</div><h1>More Riders.<br/><span class="accent">Stronger Community.</span></h1><p class="lede" style="color:#e5e8eb">Events are how we intend to bring riders, local businesses, and community partners together to support the GEAR mission.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="wrap"><div class="eyebrow accent">Planned event concepts</div><h2>Get in GEAR. Show Up.</h2><figure class="editorial-photo"><img src="/images/motorcycle-community-coffee-shop-meetup.jpg" alt="Motorcyclists meeting for coffee beside parked motorcycles at an outdoor café." loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1672" height="941"/><figcaption>Our planned community events bring riders and local businesses together. Illustrative image.</figcaption></figure><div class="cards">
<article class="card"><h3>Bikes &amp; Burritos</h3><p>Rotating Tuesday gatherings with local taco and burrito restaurants. Participating venues may support the foundation through clearly disclosed charitable sales promotions.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Bikes &amp; Brews</h3><p>Community meetups at coffee shops and roasters. “Brews” refers to coffee and nonalcoholic beverages in official GEAR programming.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>GEAR Nights</h3><p>Motorcycle shop, dealership, and community bike nights featuring rider connections, safety resources, and mission-aligned sponsors.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Kickstands Up</h3><p>Noncompetitive community rides with rider briefings, safety planning, route leaders, and appropriate event safeguards.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>GEAR Rally</h3><p>A proposed annual signature gathering celebrating riders and raising support for the foundation's four pillars.</p></article>
</div><div class="program-callout"><strong>Event status:</strong> These are planned formats, not announced events. Dates, venues, sponsors, and registration will be published only after confirmation.</div><div class="actions"><a class="btn btn-red" href="/contact/">Discuss Hosting an Event</a></div></div></section>
</Base>